    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54-a3">

                <pb facs="0213" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg85"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 322.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of a conference with President
                        Barrios.</hi></head>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Concentration of forces on the frontier not with intent to invade unless
                        in danger of being invaded.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>In accordance with article 1 of the decree of February 28, I will begin to
                        protect and sustain all works, operations, and movements directed to promote
                        the union of Central America.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Having received a cablegram from the President of Mexico, in which he
                        tells me his Government will take action, and I am disposed to repel force
                        by force should it be carried out.</item>
                    <label>(4)</label>
                    <item>Honduras will assume the same conduct, and if the Nicaraguans ask for
                        arms, they will be given them as well as money, in accordance with same
                        article 1 of said decree.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 12,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
